{"reasoning": "REST APIs and GraphQL APIs differ in their approach to data retrieval and manipulation. REST APIs follow a request-response model, where clients send HTTP requests to retrieve or modify data, whereas GraphQL APIs use a query language to specify exactly what data is needed, reducing the amount of data transferred and improving performance. GraphQL APIs also provide a more flexible and dynamic way to retrieve data, allowing for more complex queries and relationships between data points.",

 "final_answer": "REST APIs and GraphQL APIs have distinct design principles and use cases, with REST APIs typically used for simple, resource-based APIs and GraphQL APIs suited for more complex, data-driven applications.",

